stream
BT /F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 780.0 Tm (Grammar in Action) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 764.0 Tm (A learner's grammar handout) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 748.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 732.0 Tm (1. Present Perfect vs Past Simple) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 716.0 Tm (   Summary: Use present perfect for unfinished time and past simple for a finished time.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 700.0 Tm (   Example: I have lived here for ten years. / I lived there for ten years.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 684.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 668.0 Tm (2. Present Perfect Continuous) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 652.0 Tm (   Summary: An action that started in the past and is still happening, with a visible result.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 636.0 Tm (   Example: She has been painting the kitchen all morning.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 620.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 604.0 Tm (3. Past Perfect) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 588.0 Tm (   Summary: The earlier of two past events, the 'past in the past'.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 572.0 Tm (   Example: When we arrived, the film had already started.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 556.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 540.0 Tm (4. Future Continuous) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 524.0 Tm (   Summary: An action in progress at a point in the future.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 508.0 Tm (   Example: This time tomorrow I will be flying to Lisbon.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 492.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 476.0 Tm (5. Future Perfect) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 460.0 Tm (   Summary: Something completed before a point in the future.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 444.0 Tm (   Example: By Friday we will have finished the report.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 428.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 412.0 Tm (6. First Conditional) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 396.0 Tm (   Summary: A real possible situation and its result.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 380.0 Tm (   Example: If it rains, we will stay inside.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 364.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 348.0 Tm (7. Second Conditional) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 332.0 Tm (   Summary: An imaginary or unlikely present situation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 316.0 Tm (   Example: If I won the lottery, I would travel the world.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 300.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 284.0 Tm (8. Third Conditional) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 268.0 Tm (   Summary: An impossible past situation and its imagined result.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 252.0 Tm (   Example: If I had studied, I would have passed.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 236.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 220.0 Tm (9. Mixed Conditionals) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 204.0 Tm (   Summary: A past condition with a present result, or vice versa.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 188.0 Tm (   Example: If I had taken the job, I would be rich now.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 172.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 156.0 Tm (10. Passive Voice Present) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 140.0 Tm (   Summary: The object becomes the subject; the doer is optional.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 124.0 Tm (   Example: The letter is written by Maria.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 108.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 92.0 Tm (11. Passive Voice Past) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 76.0 Tm (   Summary: Past events in the passive emphasize what happened.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 60.0 Tm (   Example: The bridge was built in 1890.) Tj
ET
endstream
