6 0 obj
<< /Length 2605 >>
stream
BT /F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 780.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 764.0 Tm (12. Modal Verbs of Obligation) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 748.0 Tm (   Summary: Must, have to and should for different strengths of duty.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 732.0 Tm (   Example: You must wear a seat belt.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 716.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 700.0 Tm (13. Modal Verbs of Deduction) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 684.0 Tm (   Summary: Must, might and can't for how sure we are.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 668.0 Tm (   Example: She must be at home; her car is here.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 652.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 636.0 Tm (14. Defining Relative Clauses) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 620.0 Tm (   Summary: Which/who that identifies the noun, no commas.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 604.0 Tm (   Example: The man who called is my uncle.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 588.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 572.0 Tm (15. Non-defining Relative Clauses) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 556.0 Tm (   Summary: Extra information about a known noun, with commas.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 540.0 Tm (   Example: My brother, who lives in Oslo, is a pilot.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 524.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 508.0 Tm (16. Reported Speech) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 492.0 Tm (   Summary: Telling someone what another person said, with a tense shift.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 476.0 Tm (   Example: She said that she was tired.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 460.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 444.0 Tm (17. Indirect Questions) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 428.0 Tm (   Summary: A question inside a statement, with statement word order.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 412.0 Tm (   Example: I wonder where they live.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 396.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 380.0 Tm (18. Wish plus Past Simple) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 364.0 Tm (   Summary: To regret or want a different present.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 348.0 Tm (   Example: I wish I had a car.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 332.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 316.0 Tm (19. If only) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 300.0 Tm (   Summary: A stronger wish, often with regret.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 284.0 Tm (   Example: If only I had known earlier.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 268.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 252.0 Tm (20. Used to and Would) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 236.0 Tm (   Summary: Past habits; would only for repeated actions.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 220.0 Tm (   Example: We used to play in the park.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 204.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 188.0 Tm (21. Gerund or Infinitive) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 172.0 Tm (   Summary: Some verbs take -ing, others take to, some both.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 156.0 Tm (   Example: I enjoy reading. / I want to read.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 140.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 124.0 Tm (22. Bare Infinitive) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 108.0 Tm (   Summary: After modals and let, make, help the to drops.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 92.0 Tm (   Example: Let me help you.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 76.0 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 60.0 Tm (23. Comparatives and Superlatives) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
7 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 6 0 R >>
